{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>When you build a new house.</b> This section is attached after they fought and are in the land; it begins with the commandment of the house." "<b>A parapet.</b> Its meaning is known from the root עקה, and it has no cognate. One who is precise derives it from the root of עקת רשע, and he brings himself into distress [עקה]." "<b>The one who falls.</b> It is called by its outcome, and likewise 'the dead shall be put to death,' and likewise 'you shall strip the garments of the naked,' and 'the children shall dash.' And many phrases beyond number are called by their outcome, and we do not know whether this is the way of the language, or whether it is prophetic speech, like 'and he pursued as far as Dan,' 'as far as the Valley of Eshcol,' 'therefore a man leaves his father and his mother.' And after the commandment of the house comes the commandment of the seed and the planting, for after he is in the land and has built a house, he plants."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra rejects a forced etymology proposed by another interpreter; the parenthetical (ס״א מהמקום) is a variant-note indicating an alternate reading 'from the place.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:20.642911609Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}